  },
  {
   "v": "police",
   "t": "英語の百科事典の会社だってさ。",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "\"'They say it is an English encyclopedia company.' Native Japanese calls an encyclopedia \" Starting off with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "police",
   "t": "百科事典",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", literally a 'hundred-subjects word-book'. Ending with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "police",
   "t": "だってさ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " passes along gossip—'so I hear'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "police",
   "t": "最近はやってるみたいだな。",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Looks like that business is popular lately.'  Check out ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "police",
   "t": "はやってる",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " comes from the verb meaning to be trendy or booming, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "police",
   "t": "みたい",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " adds 'it seems like'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "muranishi",
   "t": "課長、何かあったんですか？",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "\"'Chief, did something happen?' Walk into any noisy crowd or office commotion and ask \" The phrase contains ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "muranishi",
   "t": "何かあったんですか",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", and this word is built from ",
